  "text": "\r\n         Town of Milford, NH -  \r\n     Skip to main content \r\nDepartments \nMain Menu  /  Departments \nDepartments \nAll Departments \nADA Compliance \nAmbulance \nAssessing \nBuilding Safety \nCommunity Development \nCommunity Media \nFinance \nFire Department \nHealth Department \nHuman Resources \nInformation Technology \nLibrary \nEmergency Management \nPlanning and GIS \nPolice Department \nPublic Works \nRecreation \nRecycling & Transfer Station \nStormwater Management \nTax Collection \nTown Administrator \nTown Clerk \nWater Utilities \nWelfare Department \nBoards \nMain Menu  /  Boards \nBoards \nAll Boards \nArtWalk Committee \nBudget Advisory Committee \nCemetery Trustees \nCIP Citizens Advisory Committee \nConservation Commission \nEconomic Development Advisory Council \nEnergy Advisory Committee \nEthics Committee \nGranite Town Media Advisory Committee \nHeritage Commission \nJoint Loss Management Committee \nLibrary Trustees \nMACC Base \nMaster Plan Steering Committee \nPlanning Board \nRecreation Commission \nRecycling Committee \nSelect Board \nTraffic Safety Committee \nTrustees of the Trust Fund \nVietnam Memorial Committee \nWater and Sewer Commissioners \nZoning Board of Adjustement \n250th Celebration Committee \nTown Government \nMain Menu  /  Town Government \nTown Government \nAbout Milford \nDepartments \nBoards \nElected Officials \nEmployment \nMinutes & Agendas \nActive Projects \nMunicipal Codes \nMaps / GIS Mapping \nContact Us \nResidents \nMain Menu  /  Residents \nResidents \nPermits, Forms & Links \nDepartment Directory \nUtility & Service Providers \nCommunity Power \nE Services & Payments \nVolunteer Opportunities \nSchools \nLibrary \nCemeteries \nNews & Public Notices \nCommunity Calendar \nBusiness \nMain Menu  /  Business \nBusiness \nLocal Business Organizations \nStarting a Business \nState & Regional Resources                                  \r\n                             Resources \r\n                             Calendar \r\n2026 Election/Budget Information \r\n                             2026 Election/Budget Information \r\ncontent \nThe State Primary Election is scheduled for  Tuesday,\nSeptember 8,  with polls open from 6:00 a.m. to 8:00 p.m. \nVoting Place: \n100 West St, Milford, NH 03055 \nMilford High School \n Registered voters may\nverify their party affiliation through the New Hampshire Voter Information\nPortal. Qualified voters may obtain absentee ballots by submitting an\napplication with a photocopy of identification by mail, delivering the\napplication in person to the Town Clerk, or having the application notarized. \ncontent \n2025 Voter Turnout Summary \nTotal Registered\nVoters:  10,935 \nTotal Votes\nCast:  2,833 \nFinal Turnout\nPercentage:  25.9%  of registered voters  \nResources \nResources \nResources \nCalendar \nElection Calendar \nCalendar              \r\n1 Union Square, Milford, NH 03055 \n6032490600  |  web@milford.nh.gov \nPowered By  Munibit  | © 2026 Terms  |  Privacy  |  Notifications  |  Accessibility Login                  \r\nSection Tools \r\n                         Manage Meeting Series \r\nHello  \r\nWhat is a Passkey? \n                Imagine signing into your account as easily as unlocking your phone—no more worrying about remembering or typing a password. A passkey is a secure digital key that uses the safety features in your device to keep your account protected. It’s designed to be both simple to use and highly secure. \n                Ready to experience a simpler, safer sign-in? Click the button above to create your passkey now. \r\nSign Up for Notifications! \r\n             Do not show again \r\nFill out the following fields. \n                     Activate notifications by clicking or tapping on the verification messages we send. Completing the verification process confirms your consent. Notification categories can be edited later from an email message footer. \r\n ",
